| `scripts/child_exec.py` | The shell side of `scripts/child_env.py`: a shell script's first command, `REEXEC_LINE`, hands the script here, and this module starts the same file again, by its path under its `#!` interpreter, under the environment `build_child_env` builds plus `KEEL_CHILD_ENV` set to its own pid, so the body runs once under the allowlist. | the first command of a shell script; check_X holds every script to the line | [`child_env.names`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Defence-in-depth, not a sandbox. A credential pattern that cannot compile because of syntax, recursion or overflow exits CONFIG naming the key and label, without pattern or compiler text, before any script body runs. Not for a Python spawn, which passes `env=build_child_env(...)` itself. The re-run uses the `#!` interpreter, not the shell that first ran the file; one Python start per script; stdlib-only and 3.6-safe, because the line runs the host `python3`. | [shell-style.md](../guides/shell-style.md) | always |
